# tally 2.3.1 R1, N245.21 (L §5.14 `same`'s two days, §4.4 a reader by its ends): two planned movements stated
# same with equal amounts on two known days are the hole between the days (b07) and known after both (b31:
# 600.00 PLN); before the first, the balance stands (b01); the day itself stays the hole (dy). Before: b31 the
# HOLE-SAME hole.
=== same2.tally
model same2
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input a1: money PLN
input d1: date
input d2: date
move in1: transfers
  on d1
  leg cash from world to konto amount a1
move in2: transfers
  on d2
  leg cash from world to konto amount a1
ask b01: bal(konto, 2026-03-01)
ask b07: bal(konto, 2026-03-07)
ask b31: bal(konto, 2026-03-31)
ask f1: flows(in1, 2026-03)
ask c0: count(m in transfers over 2026-03)
ask c4: count(m in transfers over 2026-04)
ask dy: m.day for m in transfers over 2026-03
version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  opening[konto] = 500.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
  a1 = 100.00 PLN "s"
  d1 = 2026-03-05 "s"
  d2 = 2026-03-10 "s"
  same in1 = in2
=== expect
b01: 500.00 PLN
  cut 2026-01-01
b07: ?"in1 and in2 are one, but leg cash differs on 2026-03-05, 2026-03-10: 100.00 PLN (in1) and 100.00 PLN (in2)" (in1, in2)
  cut 2026-01-01
b31: 600.00 PLN
  cut 2026-01-01
c0: 1
  cut 2026-01-01
c4: 0
  cut 2026-01-01
dy (m = in1): ?"in1 and in2 are one, but the day of cash differs on 2026-03-05: 2026-03-05 (in1) and 2026-03-10 (in2)" (in1, in2)
  cut 2026-01-01
f1: 100.00 PLN
  cut 2026-01-01
